se" id="qrTree18"><div class="qr-box text-center shadow-sm w-100 mt-2"><img data-tree="18" class="img-fluid dynamic-qr" alt="QR Code"><p class="small text-muted mt-1 mb-0 fw-bold">Scan to Share</p></div></div></div><div class="col-md-7 mb-3"><h6 class="fw-bold text_blue">About the Tree</h6><p class="small text-muted">The leaves, tender pods, and seeds become edible when boiled. Due to its high biomass production, this tree is planted as a dense shelterbelt. Sandalwood, a parasitic tree, often utilises it as a host species.</p><a href="https://maps.app.goo.gl/JVSXZZjeKHY9o8kk9" target="_blank" class="btn btn-sm btn-primary rounded-pill mt-3 w-100"><i class="bi bi-geo-alt-fill me-1"></i> View on Campus Map</a></div></div></div></div></div></div>
